lesson: 146
title: A rectangle's area from its perimeter
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: The perimeter of a rectangle is twice the length plus twice the width, so half the perimeter is length + width.
explain: If the perimeter is 26 cm and the length is 8 cm, then length + width = 26 ÷ 2 = 13, the width is 13 - 8 = 5 cm, and the area is 8 × 5 = 40 square centimetres.
explain: If instead the length is 3 cm more than the width: 13 - 3 = 10, 10 ÷ 2 = 5 is the width, 5 + 3 = 8 the length.
vars: a=name w=2..18 l=3..30
need: l > w
let: P = 2 * (l + w)
answer: l * w
exercise: A rectangle has a perimeter of {P} cm. Its length is {l} cm. What is its area in square centimetres?
exercise: The perimeter of a rectangle is {P} cm and its width is {w} cm. Find its area in square centimetres.
exercise: A fence {P} m long goes all around a rectangular garden. The garden is {l} m long. What is the area of the garden in square metres?
exercise: {a} made a rectangle from a wire {P} cm long. One side of the rectangle is {w} cm. What area does the rectangle cover, in square centimetres?
exercise: A rectangle has a perimeter of {P} cm, and its length is {l-w} cm more than its width. What is its area in square centimetres?
test: How many square metres is a rectangular field whose shorter side is {w} m, if walking once around it is {P} m?
test: {a} puts a ribbon of {P} cm exactly around the edge of a rectangular card. The card is {l} cm long. Find the area of the card in square centimetres.
test: The length of a rectangular room is {l-w} m greater than its width, and the room's perimeter is {P} m. What is the area of the floor in square metres?
test: A square has sides of {w} cm. A rectangle with the same width has a perimeter of {P} cm. What is the area of the rectangle in square centimetres?
exercise: Find the area, in square centimetres, of a rectangle that is {l} cm long and has a perimeter of {P} cm.
exercise: A rectangular playground in Texas is {w} m wide. The fence all around it is {P} m long. How many square metres does the playground cover?
exercise: {a} walks once around a rectangular field in Kent and covers {P} m. The field is {l} m long. What is its area in square metres?
exercise: The distance around a rectangular photo is {P} cm, and the photo is {w} cm wide. What is the area of the photo in square centimetres?
exercise: In a rectangle the width is {l-w} cm less than the length. All four sides together measure {P} cm. How many square centimetres is the area?
exercise: A farmer in Alberta puts {P} m of fencing round a rectangular pen that is {l} m long. What area does the pen have, in square metres?
exercise: Perimeter {P} cm, one side {w} cm, the other side longer: what is the area of this rectangle in square centimetres?
exercise: A rectangular rug in a house in Auckland has an edge {P} dm long all round and a length of {l} dm. What is the area of the rug in square decimetres?
test: What is the area of a rectangle, in square metres, if its shorter side is {w} m and all its sides add up to {P} m?
test: {a} needs {P} cm of tape to go once around the edge of a rectangular poster {w} cm wide. How many square centimetres is the poster?
test: A rectangular vegetable patch in Cork is {l-w} m longer than it is wide, and a path of {P} m runs right around its edge. Find its area in square metres.
test: One lap round the edge of a rectangular park in Brisbane is {P} m. Its long side is {l} m. How many square metres of land does the park take up?
test: A wooden frame {P} cm long fits exactly around a rectangular mirror whose longer side is {l} cm. What is the area of the mirror in square centimetres?
test: The perimeter of a rectangular table top is {P} dm, and the table is {l} dm long. How many square decimetres is the top?
exercise: rectangle, perimeter {P} cm, long side {l}. area?
exercise: perimeter's {P} cm, width {w+1} — no sorry, {w} cm. how many square cm is it then
exercise: my mate says the area is just {P} × {w}. nah that's wrong, what's the area of a rectangle with perimeter {P} cm and width {w} cm
exercise: garden's a rectangle, {P} m all the way round, short side {w} m, and the shed's 2 m tall but whatever. how many square metres
test: walked round the field once, {P} m. it's {l} m long. how big's the field in square metres
test: {a} says the area is {P} ÷ 2 = {l+w} square cm. reckon that's off — rectangle, perimeter {P} cm, one side {w} cm, real area?
test: fence round the yard is {P} m, yard's {w} m wide. how much ground inside, sq m
exam: It is given that a rectangle possesses a perimeter of {P} cm and a length of {l} cm. Determine the area of the said rectangle, expressed in square centimetres.
exam: Whereas the perimeter of a rectangular plot is {P} metres and its breadth is {w} metres, compute the area of the plot in square metres.
exam: Ascertain, in square centimetres, the area enclosed by a rectangle whose boundary measures {P} cm in aggregate and whose longer side measures {l} cm.
exam: Pursuant to the stipulation that a rectangular card has a perimeter of {P} cm and a shorter side of {w} cm, state the area of the card in square centimetres.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} a rectangular allotment with a perimeter of {P} m. Its length is {l} m. What is its area in square metres?
exercise: The estate agent calls the bedroom "cosy". It is a rectangle with a perimeter of {P} m and a width of {w} m. What is its area in square metres?
test: "bijou" flat my foot. the room's {P} m all round and {l} m long, so how many square metres is this bloody shoebox
